# <%~ it.instance.slug %>: Solution Architecture Document
<%
  /* Intentional consolidation (WI #269, carried into WI #318 / design v2): this
     template deliberately merges several "SAD Template.docx" viewpoint sections
     into fewer gantry modules/fields — it is NOT a 1:1 heading map to the
     reference, and that is by design. See
     docs/research/design-definition-reference-reconciliation.md §5 and §9,
     grounded in docs/reconciliation/sad-reconciliation.md.
     WI #318: `requires` is reordered end to end to match the SAD reference's
     own section order — see definition.yaml's `sad.requires` comment for the
     section-by-section rationale (dependencies moved early, open issues gets
     its own section, recovery moves before Information View, the nfrs
     performance/scalability/availability trio moves to Operating
     Considerations). `design-basis`'s optional fields are inlined here rather
     than via `_designBasisOptional.md.tmpl` — this artefact's scope is only
     `assumptions?` / `constraints?`, not the partial's full five-field set
     (that stays as-built's own shape). Blank-field guard `na()` is injected
     once as an Eta functionHeader by lib/render.js (WI #273 / R2). A
     `module.field?` requires entry is in scope but not gate-blocking (WI
     #276), so it renders as a suppress-when-blank `<% if %>` section; a bare
     entry always renders its heading via na() — including
     `glossary.terms-and-definitions`, which v1 rendered with a bare `<% if %>`
     despite being a bare (gate-blocking) requires entry. WI #331: this
     template already unified the framing and conditions clusters under one
     "# Introduction" heading — that heading now splits into "# Overview" and
     "# Design basis" (still adjacent, still first), matching the module split
     of `introduction` (retitled "Overview") and the new `design-basis`
     module. */
  const recovery = it.modules['recovery-plan'] || {}
  const dsc = it.modules['data-security-controls'] || {}
